# Village house wall, decorative and NON-solid (like railing_bg; D-041):
# whitewash w with one window per tile (green G shutters with j panel
# lines, i frame, transom and sill, b glass with s panes). Flat on purpose:
# no light top lip. Edges only use i, so a wall next to a balcony cell (the
# balcony draws the same wall behind itself) still reads as one wall:
# exposed top = i shadow under the eaves or a balcony, exposed bottom = 2 px
# i base band, exposed right = 1 px i; the left side stays lit.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_wall_village_bg
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
---
